# SWHP Frontend Implementation Tasks

This task list serves as the actionable checklist for building the SWHP React frontend using a Feature-Based Architecture and Ant Design.

## 1. Environment & Routing Setup
- [ ] Initialize the React application (`npm create vite@latest swhp-frontend`).
- [ ] Install required core dependencies (`react-router-dom`, `axios`, `antd`, `@ant-design/icons`).
- [ ] Setup the feature-based folder structure (`src/features`, `src/components`, `src/lib`, `src/config`, `src/routes`).
- [ ] Configure `axios` interceptors in `src/lib/axios.js` to handle JWT injection and centralized error handling (e.g., redirect on 401).
- [ ] Setup global routing configuration in `src/routes/` combining feature routes.

## 2. Authentication & Profile Features (`features/auth`, `features/profile`)
- [ ] Create Context API (`AuthContext`) for global session management inside `features/auth/context`.
- [ ] Build the `Login` and `Register` UI components using Ant Design `<Form>`.
- [ ] Implement legacy account mapping UI (`AccountMapping`) utilizing antd Modals/Drawers.
- [ ] Develop the `UserProfile` component inside `features/profile/components` for collecting common cross-system fields.

## 3. Service Selection Feature (`features/services`)
- [ ] Build the `ServiceList` component, rendering available legacy services using antd `<Card>` and `<Checkbox.Group>`.
- [ ] Implement custom hook `hooks/useSwan.js` to submit selected services to `/api/v1/swan/create` and store the generated SWAN.

## 4. iFrame Orchestration Feature (`features/application`)
- [ ] Create the `ServiceIframe` wrapper component for loading individual legacy forms.
- [ ] Implement the `ApplicationOrchestrator` to manage the queue, visualizing progress with antd `<Steps>`.
- [ ] Create `hooks/usePostMessage.js` to add the `window.addEventListener('message')` listener.
- [ ] Implement strict `event.origin` validation and verify the `eventType === 'FormCompleted'` and `payload.swan` match.

## 5. Payment & Tracking Features (`features/payment`, `features/tracking`)
- [ ] Build the `FeeSummary` component to fetch and display the aggregated fee breakdown from `/api/v1/swan/{swan}/fees` using antd `<Descriptions>`.
- [ ] Integrate the "Initiate Payment" redirect logic.
- [ ] Develop the `TrackingTable` dashboard using antd `<Table>` to list real-time status of submitted applications.

## 6. Security & Finalization
- [ ] Integrate CAPTCHA into public auth views.
- [ ] Ensure all forms use strict validation and handle API errors gracefully using antd `<message>` or `<notification>`.
- [ ] Verify CSRF defenses and ensure no sensitive data is placed in localStorage.
